<Legal title="Support – Anywhere, coding agent workspace" description="Help for Anywhere – Agent Remote: GitHub issues, pairing the iPhone with your Mac, and the README." path="/support">
    <article>
      <h1>Support</h1>
      <p>Anywhere on your iPhone or iPad pairs with Anywhere on your Mac. The two talk over Tailscale.</p>

      <h2>Get help</h2>
      <p>Open an issue at <a href="https://github.com/mingo023/anywhere/issues">github.com/mingo023/anywhere/issues</a>. Install, the agents the Mac app runs, and the phone app are in the <a href="https://github.com/mingo023/anywhere#ios">README</a>.</p>

      <h2>Pairing</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Install <a href="https://apps.apple.com/app/tailscale/id1470499037">Tailscale</a> on the iPhone and the Mac, and connect both. The phone app does not include Tailscale.</li>
        <li>On the Mac, open Anywhere → Settings → Phone → Pair a phone. The QR code lasts 5 minutes.</li>
        <li>On the iPhone, scan that code. Or choose Enter code instead, and type the Mac's Tailscale address and the code. Leave the port out and the app uses 4517.</li>
        <li>If the phone can't reach the Mac, check that Tailscale is connected on both and that the Mac is awake.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Privacy</h2>
      <p>How the app handles data is in the <a href="/privacy">privacy policy</a>.</p>
    </article>
</Legal>
